@page "/website-trust-scanner"
@attribute [AllowAnonymous]
@layout PublicLayout

<PageTitle>Website Trust Scanner | HIP Human-Interactive Protocol</PageTitle>
<HeadContent>
    <meta name="description" content="Check a website for HTTPS, certificate, DNS, reputation and page-risk signals with HIP's explainable website trust scanner." />
</HeadContent>

<main class="hip-public-page">
    <section class="hip-page-hero hip-grid-bg">
        <div class="hip-container">
            <p class="hip-eyebrow">Website trust scanner</p>
            <h1>Check a website before you <span>trust it.</span></h1>
            <p class="hip-lead">HIP (Human-Interactive Protocol) examines available website trust and risk signals, then presents the result with plain-language reasons. A score describes the evidence checked at that time; it is not a guarantee of safety.</p>
            <div class="hip-hero-actions">
                <a class="hip-button" href="/lookup">Scan a website</a>
                <a class="hip-button-secondary" href="/methodology">Read the scoring methodology</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="hip-section">
        <div class="hip-container">
            <div class="hip-section-heading">
                <p class="hip-eyebrow">Signals</p>
                <h2>Evidence you can inspect.</h2>
            </div>
            <div class="hip-capability-grid">
                <article><span>Connection</span><h3>HTTPS and certificates</h3><p>HIP checks encrypted transport, redirects, certificate validity, issuer details and expiry risk.</p></article>
                <article><span>Identity</span><h3>DNS and ownership</h3><p>Domain records and explicit verification evidence can establish control. Control alone does not prove trustworthiness.</p></article>
                <article><span>Risk</span><h3>Reputation and page signals</h3><p>Available reputation, content and behaviour signals contribute evidence with their source and effect explained.</p></article>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>
</main>
